NPA RoboCasa ACT runtime derivative

Upstream: RoboCasa commit 8f3c96ec8d1bfcd8126cad2bca887da98d30e997
Upstream license: MIT; its LICENSE includes a separate Apache-2.0 notice for
partial DeepMind MuJoCo code.
Upstream LICENSE SHA-256: 5da18670b3f00c59847b1ded9c28dee59940d963b1e03b528b0108d9c5a09885
Local version: 1.0.0+npa4

The local patch changes setup.py packaging metadata and one compatibility import.
It identifies the
derivative, updates RoboCasa's LeRobot dependency from 0.3.3 to the separately
reviewed 0.6.1+npa2 NPA ACT derivative, and removes tianshou 0.4.10 from the
declared closure. Exact-source inspection found tianshou is imported only by
upstream robocasa/scripts/bench_speed.py, a vectorized speed benchmark outside
the NPA service and matched ACT rollout path. That upstream benchmark script is
not qualified by this derivative. The compatibility import resolves write_info
from lerobot.datasets.io_utils, its location in the pinned LeRobot derivative,
so the native recorded-action playback module can import its data reader.
No replay function, action ordering, reset, success predicate, assets, or
simulator behavior changes. Dataset writing and unrelated upstream tools are
not qualified by this import repair. All dependencies used by the
qualified NPA service remain declared and resolver-checked.

The matched ACT path and native recorded-action reader/import controls are
checked during image construction; task success still requires actual native
rollouts. This does not
claim upstream support for LeRobot 0.6.1 or qualify other RoboCasa policy, training,
benchmark, or deployment paths.

The normal resolver closure includes qpsolvers 4.13.0 under LGPL-3.0 and
quadprog 0.1.13 under GPL-2.0-or-later. Their exact official source archives,
license texts, hashes, and redistribution notice are retained in the image.
